===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|collective}} A [[group#Noun|group]] of [[person|people]] [[hire#Verb|hired]] to [[attend]] a [[performance]] and to either [[applaud]] or [[boo#Verb|boo]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Theatre claqueurs in Vienna form union; now get two Wienerwursts for simple applause, six with beer for special ovations|newspaper=w:The New York Times|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210728165133/https://www.nytimes.com/1930/02/23/archives/theatre-claqueurs-in-vienna-form-union-now-get-two-wienerwursts-for.html|archivedate=28 July 2021|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:The New York Times Company|date=23 February 1930|page=4|column=1|issn=0362-4331|oclc=971436363|passage=The most popular singers have been obliged to give free tickets and even to donate cash, lest the '''claque''' retaliate by frantic applause at the wrong moment.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=John Briggs|title=What every young claqueur should know|newspaper=w:The New York Times|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210728181900/https://www.nytimes.com/1957/12/22/archives/what-every-young-claqueur-should-know-function.html|archivedate=28 July 2021|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:The New York Times Company|date=22 December 1957|page=53|columns=4–7|issn=0362-4331|oclc=971436363|passage=The '''claque''' isn't paid. In fact, claqueurs pay to get in. The inducement is that they can buy standing room for half price, without waiting in line.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}}
## A group of [[fawning#Adjective|fawning]] [[admirer]]s.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=05 Dec 81|volume=9|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=6|author=Michael Bronski|title=Coming (Out) to Opera|text=The most obvious gay connection to opera is the cult of the diva. Stauncher even than the fans of Garland of Striesand, the '''claques''' of Maria Callas and Joan Sutherland (among others) have been fanatical in their devotion. Going beyond the usual "appreciation stage" the fans glorify and deify their stars: Callas was "La Divina," Sutherland "La Stupenda."}}
## A group of people who [[pre-arrange]] among themselves to [[express#Verb|express]] [[strong]] [[support#Noun|support]] for an [[idea]], so as to [[give#Verb|give]] the [[false]] [[impression]] of a [[wide]]r [[consensus]].

